wikipedia_extract: USS Northampton (CL/CA-26) was the lead Northampton-class cruiser
  in service with the United States Navy. She was commissioned in 1930, originally
  classified a light cruiser because of her thin armor but later reclassified a heavy
  cruiser because of her 8-inch guns. During World War II she served in the Pacific
  and was sunk by Japanese torpedoes during the Battle of Tassafaronga on 30 November
  1942. She was named after the city of Northampton, Massachusetts, the home of former
  President Calvin Coolidge.
